title: "statement gossip: hold initial sync to the peer's statement rate limit"

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A node now serves a peer's statement backlog at the rate the peer accepts. Each peer carries
    a mirror of its statement rate limit on the send side, charged by every chunk sent, and an
    initial sync waits when the mirror has no room for a chunk. A fast peer no longer receives
    more than `statements_per_second` and disconnects the node as a flooder, and a peer that keeps
    asking for its backlog draws it at that rate.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
